From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Willie Abrams <willie@pobox.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 14:06:04 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 10/19] kk: Support transform feedback in GS emulation

Use poly's pre-GS program for geometry shaders with XFB outputs, as hk
does. Run the count shader and prefix sum first when the primitive
counts aren't known at compile time.

Keep the buffer offsets in command buffer memory. Begin reads the
supplied counters and zeros the other offsets; end writes back to the
supplied counters.

ro_to_rw_poly needs no conversion here. Send pipeline statistics to
scratch, since kk doesn't expose them.

The XFB stores run in the rasterization VS. Poly generates a bounded set
of stores and checks the stream and buffer limits before writing. Its
handling of the original GS side effects is unchanged.

Assisted-by: Claude Code
